<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-26">26 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Valentinian I proclaimed Roman Emperor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Army officers chose Valentinian, a Pannonian general, as emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a>. A month later he made his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a> co-emperor in the East, while he ruled the West.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valentinian-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-28">28 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Valentinian I makes his brother Valens co-emperor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, the Roman emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-i">Valentinian I</a> made his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a> co-Augustus, giving him the eastern half of the empire and keeping the West for himself. Valens ruled until 378, when he was killed fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> at Adrianople.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-i">Valentinian I</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
